# Names only, no values. One secret per root-only file (0600) in /etc/bulig, loaded by systemd LoadCredential= and read by the kernel
# from $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY. They are NOT in the unit's environment, so the Claude sessions a worker starts cannot inherit them.
# Set each with:  deploy/set-secret.sh --credential <name>  (value on stdin, never on a command line)
#
#   pg-url          postgres://bulig:<generated>@127.0.0.1:5436/bulig   written by setup-cluster.sh (explicit host and port)
#   gh-token        GitHub token of the bot account (Keychain item bulig-github-bot on the Mac)
#   claude-token    from `claude setup-token` for the bulig user (interactive, Jasher only)
#   worker-tokens   per-worker tokens for the remote worker protocol (PR-C); empty until that lands
#
# Added at cutover only, never before. Two kernels must never poll one Telegram bot:
#   telegram-token  Keychain item bulig-telegram-bot on the Mac (add LoadCredential=telegram-token:/etc/bulig/telegram-token to the unit)
#
# The kernel reads credentials from $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY once the worker-protocol change (PR-C / ADR 0011) lands. Until then the
# config's store.urlEnv still names BULIG_PG_URL, which this unit deliberately does not set.
